{"text": "LOS ANGELES COUNTY DISTRICT ATTORNEY\u2019S OFFICE\n\nJACKIE LACEY e District Attorney JOHN K. SPILLANE\nChief Deputy District Attorney\n\nDecember 20, 2016\n\nThe Honorable William C. Ryan\nWrit Center\nLos Angeles County Superior Court\nClara Shortridge Foltz Criminal Justice Center\n210 West Temple Street\nLos Angeles, California 90012\n\nDear Judge Ryan:\nIn re PEOPLE V. RAYMOND JENNINGS, Case No. MA033712\n\nThis document is an addendum to the June 22, 2016, letter to Judge James Brandlin which by\nstipulation of the parties, and with the approval of this court, serves as the Petition for Writ of\nHabeas Corpus by petitioner Raymond Jennings. The petition asserts that newly discovered\nevidence exists which completely undermines the prosecution\u2019s case and points unerringly to the\ninnocence of Raymond Jennings in the murder of Michelle O\u2019Keefe.!\n\nThe Los Angeles County Sheriff\u2019s Department is currently investigating the murder of Michelle\nO\u2019Keefe. Based on the investigation conducted to date, the Los Angeles County District\nAttorney\u2019s Office agrees that Raymond Jennings is entitled to relief through habeas corpus based\non newly discovered evidence pointing to his factual innocence.\n\nThe Los Angeles County District Attorney's Office has lost confidence in the validity of the\nconviction and requests that this court grant the habeas corpus petition and set aside Jennings\u2019\nconviction.\n\nAdditionally, based upon the current state of the evidence known to us, the Los Angeles County\nDistrict Attorney's Office will not seek to retry Raymond Jennings for the murder of Michelle\nO'Keefe.\n\n' See, In re Lawley (2008) 42 Cal.4th 1231, 1240-1241.\n\nHall of Justice\n211 West Temple Street\nLos Angeles, CA 90012\n(213) 257-2928",
